("p", "THEOREM I (Obstruction transport and conservation). Let P be a well-formed presentation at tolerance ε with obstruction datum (λ<sub>ε</sub>, Γ<sub>set</sub> ⊇ Γ<sub>eff</sub> ⊇ Γ<sub>B</sub>), and let F : P → Q be a morphism of presentations carrying tolerance overhead ρ, an effective translator, and resource overhead H. Then three statements hold. (i) PROVED-CORPUS: obstructions transport forward — if ε lies in the obstruction spectrum of P at any of the outcomes L, D, K, then ρ(ε) lies in the corresponding spectrum of Q, while successes transport with overhead; this is the spectrum-transport proposition of the monograph, the corpus’s own one-way valve. (ii) NEW: reflection prices relocation — if Q is unobstructed at ρ(ε) within the transported budget while P is obstructed at ε, then F is not an isomorphism of obstruction data, and the tolerance gap ρ(ε) − ε is exactly the ignorance F relocates; it vanishes if and only if F preserves and reflects all five diagnostic outcomes, which the monograph itself proves need not happen even when capability is preserved. (iii) NEW: the quantum instances are the sharp case — for an environment E of dimension e > 1, tensoring with E admits neither adjoint, the obstruction integer e<super>4</super>−e<super>2</super>+1 lies strictly between (e<super>2</super>−1)<super>2</super> and e<super>4</super>, and the minimal leakage is the adjunction defect δ(e) = e<super>2</super>−1, the dimension of su(e), obeying the multiplicative cascade law 1+δ(E⊗F) = (1+δ(E))(1+δ(F))."),
