("p", "The physical reading is the law itself. Ignorance can be moved: sensor repair moves it into the controller — the monograph’s repair coordinates price exactly this, with zero-bit repair possible only for local behaviours, message alphabets of at least two, and detector-efficiency thresholds certified by linear programs with Farkas duals. It can be refined: the refinement–resolution bridge moves it into finer spatial resolution, and the rate–distortion formula prices the refinement. It can be priced: the obstruction’s exchange rate against states is the determination index. What no exact, conservative transformation can do is destroy it — and the non-exact ones leak measurably. The leak is not metaphor: under environment decoration, the hom-dimension of the one-slot comb jumps from 204 to 3132 on the two-qubit instance, the decoration rescales the source-linear coefficient while the constant term is rigid, and the deficit e<super>2</super>−1 is precisely the non-trace-preserving directions that normalization removed. The first law of bounded observation is thus also a bookkeeping law: every transformation of a constrained system files its ignorance somewhere, and the filing is auditable."),
